# KNOWN voice gaps, one TAB-separated line each: a kind or rule, and what
# it lacks (no_witness, no_help, no_fix, no_doc, bad_fix, bad_remedy, no_remedy). This file only ever
# SHRINKS — `avra voices --baseline <this file> --accept` prunes what a
# fix made gone, and no path through it ADDS a line: a new voice gets its
# help, fix and witness in the code, or a human adds the line here,
# reviewed at adoption and every time after. `make voices` gates.
